; Regression test for the stray error context in issue #3281: a failure that
; ledger deliberately ignores must not leave its error context behind.
;
; When a posting lacks the --pivot tag, transfer_details tries the tag name
; as a posting property instead (as in `--pivot payee`) and ignores the
; failure when it is not one.  But the failed evaluation had already
; recorded "While evaluating value expression: Fund" in the global error
; context, and nothing cleared it.  The next real error -- here an unknown
; identifier in --limit -- was then reported under one stray frame for each
; posting pivoted so far.
;
; The query parser does the same with a term that only looks like a date
; comparison: `a<[b]` is tried as an expression first, and when that fails
; to parse, it is matched against account names instead.

2022-01-11 * Monthly fee
    Expenses:Fees                5.00 GBP
    Assets:Pension              -5.00 GBP

test bal --pivot Fund -l 'nosuch' -> 1
__ERROR__
While evaluating value expression:
  nosuch
  ^^^^^^
While handling posting from "$FILE", line 17:
>     Expenses:Fees                5.00 GBP
Error: Unknown identifier 'nosuch'
end test

test bal 'a<[b]' -l 'nosuch' -> 1
__ERROR__
While evaluating value expression:
  (nosuch & (account =~ /a<[b]/))
   ^^^^^^
While handling posting from "$FILE", line 17:
>     Expenses:Fees                5.00 GBP
Error: Unknown identifier 'nosuch'
end test
